-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Long-Duration Scenes:** Excessively long-duration inputs may struggle to fit data adequately with a small number of parameters ($B=512, T=512$) [S1].
-*   **No Deformation Field (SLS4Dnd):** Removing the deformation field leads to a decline in reconstruction quality due to the lack of decoupling between time and space [S1].
-*   **No Time Slots (SLS4Dnf):** Removing time slots results in degradation of rendering quality, as they ensure smoothness of dense temporal information [S1].
-*   **Decoder Choice:** Using only GeLU (SLS4Dge) or a standard MLP (SLS4Dml) as the interpolator decoder results in inferior performance compared to GeGLU [S1].
-*   **Learning Rate:** Using only cosine decay (SLS4Dco) is unstable; using only exponential decay (SLS4Deo) may get stuck in local optima [S1].
+### Parameters
+*   **B (Number of latent features):** 512 [S1].
+*   **T (Number of time slots):** 512 [S1].
+*   **Learning Rate Decay:** Cosine*exp decay function. Cosine decay alone is unstable; exponential decay alone may get stuck in local optima [S1].
+
+### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
+*   **Long-duration inputs:** Excessively long-duration inputs may struggle to fit data adequately with a small number of parameters [S1].
+*   **Absence of deformation fields:** Without deformation fields (SLS4Dnd), the absence of decoupling between time and space poses challenges in extracting information for reconstruction [S1].
+*   **Removing time slots:** Removing time slots (SLS4Dnf) results in degradation of rendering quality [S1].
+*   **Decoder choice:** Using only GeLU (SLS4Dge) or MLP (SLS4Dml) as interpolator decoder results in inferior performance compared to GeGLU [S1].
 
